concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Establishment and appointment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(1) There is to be a Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control. Appointment by Minister (2) The Director-General is to be appointed by the Minister, by written instrument. (3) The Minister must not appoint a person as the Director-General unless satisfied that the person has appropriate expertise, qualifications or experience in public health matters. Period of appointment (4) The Director-General holds office for a period of 5 years unless a shorter period is specified in the instrument of appointment. Note: The Director-General may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) There is to be a Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control. Appointment by Minister (2) The Director-General is to be appointed by the Minister, by written instrument. (3) The Minister must not appoint a person as the Director-General unless satisfied that the person has appropriate expertise, qualifications or experience in public health matters. Period of appointment (4) The Director-General holds office for a period of 5 years unless a shorter period is specified in the instrument of appointment. Note: The Director-General may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ebbd93eeece69296d879d5eea8ffba0995e930ba033e9bb8c8fa566c63e9d7f7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-10-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-10-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-10-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-10-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.21" .
doc:sec-10 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10 Establishment and appointment" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) There is to be a Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control. Appointment by Minister (2) The Director-General is to be appointed by the Minister, by written instrument. (3) The Minister must not appoint a person as the Director-General unless satisfied that the person has appropriate expertise, qualifications or experience in public health matters. Period of appointment (4) The Director-General holds office for a period of 5 years unless a shorter period is specified in the instrument of appointment. Note: The Director-General may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer .

