concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13 Powers of the Director-General"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-13 ;
    values:originalText "Necessary or convenient power (1) The Director-General has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance of the Director-General’s functions and duties. Entering into agreements (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the Director-General may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into an agreement with any of the following if the agreement relates to the functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the Centre: (a) a State; (b) a Territory; (c) a State or Territory government entity. Entering into arrangements (3) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the Director-General may, on behalf of the Centre, enter into an arrangement with any of the following if the arrangement relates to the functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the Centre: (a) a foreign government body; (b) an international organisation; (c) an international partnership.   The Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2 The Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3 Section 14 No. 61, 2025 Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025" ;
    skos:definition "Necessary or convenient power (1) The Director-General has power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for, or in connection with, the performance of the Director-General’s functions and duties. Entering into agreements (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the Director-General may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, enter into an agreement with any of the following if the agreement relates to the functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the Centre: (a) a State; (b) a Territory; (c) a State or Territory government entity. Entering into arrangements (3) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the Director-General may, on behalf of the Centre, enter into an arrangement with any of the following if the arrangement relates to the functions, duties or powers of the Director-General or the Centre: (a) a foreign government body; (b) an international organisation; (c) an international partnership.   The Australian Centre for Disease Control  Part 2 The Director-General of the Australian Centre for Disease Control  Division 3 Section 14 No. 61, 2025 Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1659f9566572d0ed399e4ae12b4316b19fdba40e523bfa40db0c0c4f82a45506" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-13-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025.pdf, p.24" .
