    values:originalText "(6) A data sharing declaration is a legislative instrument, but section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the declaration. 68  When data sharing declarations cease to be in force A data sharing declaration ceases to be in force at the earliest of the following: (a) if a time at which the declaration will cease to be in force is specified in the declaration—at that time; (b) the time at which the declaration is repealed; (c) the start of the day after the end of the period of 12 months beginning on the day the declaration commences." ;
