doc:sec-71-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "71(1) Unauthorised use or disclosure of protected information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and (b) the person has obtained or generated information in the course of or for the purposes of: (i) performing functions or duties, or exercising powers, under this Act; or (ii) assisting another person to perform functions or duties, or exercise powers, under this Act; or (iii) providing data services to the Director-General; or (iv) receiving information given in accordance with a request or agreement under subsection 43(1) or a direction under subsection 45(1); and (c) the information is protected information; and (d) the person uses or discloses the information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-71-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "71(2) Unauthorised use or disclosure of protected information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-71-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and (b) the person has obtained information as a result of a disclosure under section 51 made for the purpose of assisting the person, or another person, to perform a function or duty, or exercise a power, under: (i) the National Health Security Act 2007; or (ii) the National Occupational Respiratory Disease Registry Act 2023; and (c) the information is protected information; and (d) the person uses or discloses the information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.   Information  Part 4 Unauthorised use or disclosure of information  Division 4 Section 71 No. 61, 2025 Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 Person employed or engaged by prescribed public health entity that is a Commonwealth entity" ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and (b) the person has obtained information as a result of a disclosure under section 51 made for the purpose of assisting the person, or another person, to perform a function or duty, or exercise a power, under: (i) the National Health Security Act 2007; or (ii) the National Occupational Respiratory Disease Registry Act 2023; and (c) the information is protected information; and (d) the person uses or discloses the information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.   Information  Part 4 Unauthorised use or disclosure of information  Division 4 Section 71 No. 61, 2025 Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 Person employed or engaged by prescribed public health entity that is a Commonwealth entity"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "64f18238d9a40a57778e7e320cd4797e0030289c15dd8297a92aabd8ff701da8" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-centre-for-disease-control-act-2025-sec-71 ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Unauthorized use or disclosure of protected information is prohibited." ;
